# ANCHORING POLICY — read before adding a pattern.
#
# A trailing-slash pattern with no leading slash matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth. That is correct for caches, which appear throughout the
# tree, and catastrophic for anything that shares a name with a source package:
# "data/" and "models/" silently swallowed src/data and src/models, so
# golden.py, scorecard.py, cvat_ingest.py and preprocess.py were excluded from
# their own commits and a fresh clone could not import them.
#
# Rule: if the directory exists at exactly one known place, ANCHOR it with a
# leading slash. Only patterns that must match at every depth are left
# unanchored, and each is marked below. Anchoring those would be a regression —
# it would stop ignoring caches inside src/ and fill git status with them.

# Virtual environments — root only.
# .venv-infinigen is deliberately absent from this list as of Day 18: that
# toolchain now lives outside the repo tree (sibling directory), and
# scripts/env_gate.py's stray-venv scan should never find one in-tree again.
/venv/
/.venv/
/.venv-pinned/

# Editor / IDE state — machine-local, not shared engineering config. Root only.
/.vscode/

# Generated pipeline artifacts. These are run outputs, not source: they are
# reproducible from the code plus a run manifest, and committing them makes
# diffs unreviewable and the clone large.
#
# Every pattern below is ANCHORED with a leading slash. Unanchored, "data/"
# matches a directory named data at ANY depth, so it silently swallowed the
# src/data and src/models source packages: golden.py, scorecard.py,
# cvat_ingest.py and preprocess.py were all excluded from their commits and a
# fresh clone could not import them. Keep the leading slash.
/outputs/
/output/
/logs/

# Model weights and exported IR — fetched via scripts/fetch_weights.py
/models/

# Downloaded datasets — content-addressed by scripts/fetch_dataset.py
/data/

# Python build / cache.
# UNANCHORED DELIBERATELY — these occur at every depth of the tree and must be
# ignored wherever they appear. None of them can collide with a source package
# name, which is what makes leaving them unanchored safe.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Root-only build and coverage artifacts.
/build/
/dist/
/.coverage
/coverage.xml
/htmlcov/
